# What a real WordPress install of this plugin never needs — kept out of
# chapterwright.zip and out of whatever gets committed to the WordPress.org
# SVN repo. Mirrors the exclude list in AGENTS.md's release checklist;
# keep the two in sync if either changes.
#
# tests/ in particular must stay out of the shipped plugin: tests/bootstrap.php
# is a PHPUnit bootstrap that intentionally runs *before* WordPress core (and
# therefore ABSPATH) is loaded, so it can never carry the usual
# "if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) exit;" guard — a static "does this file
# guard against direct access" scan run against the raw source tree will
# always flag it. That's expected and does not need a code fix; excluding
# tests/ from the actual submission is the fix.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.distignore
.wp-env.json
.npmrc
node_modules
vendor
tests
admin/app/src
package.json
package-lock.json
composer.json
composer.lock
phpcs.xml.dist
phpunit.xml.dist
chapterwright.zip
coverage
.phpunit.cache
.phpcs-cache
*.log
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.idea
.vscode
AGENTS.md
TODO.md
.agents
.codex
.claude
.cursor
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
